WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.720
A long couch.

2
00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.350
Curtains blowing.

3
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.400
A woman in a white dress.

4
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:08.530
Around her stand three men: the narrator,

5
00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.740
her husband, and the man she loved before.

6
00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.240
Each holds up a different picture of her.

7
00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:19.260
She tells the narrator she hopes her
daughter will be "a beautiful little fool".

8
00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:22.390
Daisy is often blamed for Gatsby's death.

9
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.740
Is that fair?

10
00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.930
In this mission, you'll ask
whose eyes we see Daisy through,

11
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.930
and what that does to her.

12
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.000
You'll hear what Nick decides
about that voice of hers.

13
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.760
And you'll weigh critics who
have read her as a villain,

14
00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:36.490
and as a victim.

15
00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:40.280
Your mission: decide whether
blaming Daisy is fair.
